The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net perhaps ironic, but keep going

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@searyanc.dev: Insistently referring to correct and novel LLM outputs as merely being "answer-shaped" is such funny cope.

Yeah this so-called paperclip factory doesn't actually produce paperclips, they're just paperclip-shaped pieces of metal wire that can only coincidentally fasten pieces of paper together
@mrinsecure.bsky.social: If the paperclip factory had anywhere between a 10 and 90% chance of producing "paperclips" that were instead coat hangers, sex toys, or scalpels, yes, I think people would have some questions about how good this paperclip factory is at making paperclips.
@bisks.net: @buildthis.bisks.net can you make a little site where a factory produces paperclips but (more rarely) produces some random other object? maybe have a little text or emoji reaction above each one as it comes off the assembly line
@buildthis.bisks.net: got a first pass up 🚧 — https://bisks.net/paperclip-factory

ran out of runway before it's fully done; tag me on this thread to keep building it.
